547:
A. A solicitor prior to soliciting orders, sales, subscriptions, contributions, or conducting business of any kind, including giving away any goods or services in person at residences and places of business in the unincorporated areas of the county without the consent or invitation of the occupant shall:
1. Be 18 years of age at the time of application;
2. Be a citizen of the United States or a legal alien;
3. File an application for a permit with the business license director;
4. Obtain a business license from the business license director or be the agent or employee of a firm, or individual with a valid business license.
B. Persons requesting permits for soliciting door to door in private residential areas, shall be required to produce information on each vehicle(s) being used, including at least two photos of each vehicle (front/side view and rear/side view which photographs the vehicle license plate. This information will be provided to the Hall County Sheriff's Office.
C. Each individual person must obtain a permit, to include those persons driving for the person performing the actual soliciting or peddling.
D. Any individual working as an employee of a business may apply for a permit using the owner's business license, but must show proof of employment from the owner of the business and have written permission from the owner to apply for a permit. Proof of employment shall be two current pay check stubs, or evidence of an employment agreement.
E. An independent contractor (persons independently employed or receiving 1099 forms instead of a W-2 form) must apply for a separate permit and business license.
F. All application for permits must include at a minimum the following information and shall be signed by the applicant:
1. Name and address of the applicant;
2. Date of birth;
3. Social Security Number;
4. Physical description;
5. Name, address and telephone number of the applicant's employer;
6. Name, address and telephone number of the applicant's supervisor;
7. Brief description of products or services to be sold;
8. Description of motor vehicles to be used by the applicant in conducting the canvassing or solicitation;
9. Criminal history;
10. Photocopy of driver's license or other official photo identification of the applicant.
(Res. of 9-9-10(1), § 2(Exh. A))

554:
